; Interprets: 3GPP TS 29.273
;; What TS 29.273's clauses state in prose about an AVP's value or presence,
;; read by hand and pinned to the sentences read (docs/constraints.md), in
;; clause order: per interface, the conditions of the information-element
;; tables' C rows, scoped to the command each table describes, then the
;; interface's AVP clauses. A clause pointing at another document for a
;; layout is an `element`; a rule depending on an earlier message, a
;; feature, the node, the subscription or the procedure is `text-only`.
;;
;; The document prints Diameter-EAP-Request and -Answer for SWa with no
;; application, for STa and SWd under STa's 16777250, and S6b's AA-Request
;; and -Answer twice under 16777272: `; Command-Section:` names the print a
;; table describes, as the corrections attaching the tables do. A condition
;; only the first answer of a procedure meets, or only a re-authentication's
;; answer sharing that print, is `text-only` where reading it as a rule
;; would refuse the other procedure's answer.
;;
;; Release 18 prints a reference to another 3GPP document as "3GPP TS",
;; Release 19 as "TS": a quote ends before such a reference, which an
;; `element` rule names, so that one block reads both copies.


;; SWa, clause 4: the tables of clause 4.1.2, describing the
;; Diameter-EAP-Request and -Answer printed in clause 4.2.2.1 with no
;; application.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: swa-der-transport-access-type
; AVP: Transport-Access-Type
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Request
; Command-Section: 4.2.2.1.1
; Section: 4.1.2.1.1
; Table: 4.1.2.1/1
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"if the access network needs to receive the IMSI of the UE in the authentication response, then this information element shall be present, and it shall contain the value \"BBF\" (see clause 5.2.3.19)."
    text-only


;; AUTHORIZE_AUTHENTICATE is 3 (IETF RFC 6733 clause 8.7).
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: swa-der-auth-request-type
; AVP: Auth-Request-Type
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Request
; Command-Section: 4.2.2.1.1
; Section: 4.1.2.1.1
; Table: 4.1.2.1/1
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"AUTHORIZE_AUTHENTICATE shall be used in this case."
    range 3


;; The method is the access network's choice, and clause 4.1.2.1.2 has
;; the AAA server select it by ANID's presence: no message shows it
;; apart from the AVP itself.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: swa-der-anid
; AVP: ANID
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Request
; Command-Section: 4.2.2.1.1
; Section: 4.1.2.1.1
; Table: 4.1.2.1/1
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"It shall be included if the non-3GPP access network selects the EAP-AKA' authentication method."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: swa-der-high-priority-access-info
; AVP: High-Priority-Access-Info
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Request
; Command-Section: 4.2.2.1.1
; Section: 4.1.2.1.1
; Table: 4.1.2.1/1
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This information element shall be sent to the 3GPP AAA Server if the UE has access priority"
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: swa-dea-auth-request-type
; AVP: Auth-Request-Type
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Command-Section: 4.2.2.1.2
; Section: 4.1.2.1.1
; Table: 4.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"It shall contain the value AUTHORIZE_AUTHENTICATE."
    range 3


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: swa-dea-eap-master-session-key
; AVP: EAP-Master-Session-Key
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Command-Section: 4.2.2.1.2
; Section: 4.1.2.1.1
; Table: 4.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This IE shall be present if the Result-Code AVP is set to DIAMETER_SUCCESS."
    present-if Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: swa-dea-redirect-host
; AVP: Redirect-Host
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Command-Section: 4.2.2.1.2
; Section: 4.1.2.1.1
; Table: 4.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This information element shall be present if the Result-Code value is set to DIAMETER_REDIRECT_INDICATION."
    present-if Result-Code = DIAMETER_REDIRECT_INDICATION


;; UNTRUSTED is 1 (clause 5.2.3.9). The SWa print's header names no
;; application, so traffic under STa's 16777250 is held to STa's and
;; SWd's prints: the rule holds of the print as read.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: swa-dea-an-trusted
; AVP: AN-Trusted
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Command-Section: 4.2.2.1.2
; Section: 4.1.2.1.1
; Table: 4.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"For the SWa case, the value \"UNTRUSTED\" shall be used."
    range 1


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: swa-dea-mobile-node-identifier
; AVP: Mobile-Node-Identifier
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Command-Section: 4.2.2.1.2
; Request-Section: 4.2.2.1.1
; Section: 4.1.2.1.1
; Table: 4.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This information element shall only be sent if the Result-Code AVP is set to DIAMETER_SUCCESS and if the Transport Access Type in the request command indicated that the UE is accessing the EPC from a Fixed Broadband access network"
    requires Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS
    requires request/Transport-Access-Type = BBF
"This IE shall not include the leading digit prepended in front of the IMSI used to differentiate between authentication schemes."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: swa-dea-mps-priority
; AVP: MPS-Priority
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Command-Section: 4.2.2.1.2
; Section: 4.1.2.1.1
; Table: 4.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This information element shall be sent to the non-3GPP WLAN access if the UE has an MPS subscription in the HSS."
    text-only


;; AUTHORIZE_AUTHENTICATE is 1 (IETF RFC 6733 clause 8.12).
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: swa-rar-re-auth-request-type
; AVP: Re-Auth-Request-Type
; Command: Re-Auth-Request
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 4.2.2.4.1
; Section: 4.1.2.4.1
; Table: 4.1.2.4.1/1
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"AUTHORIZE_AUTHENTICATE shall be used in this case."
    range 1


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: swa-reauth-der-high-priority-access-info
; AVP: High-Priority-Access-Info
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Request
; Command-Section: 4.2.2.1.1
; Section: 4.1.2.4.1
; Table: 4.1.2.4.1/3
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This information element shall be sent to the 3GPP AAA Server if the UE has access priority"
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: swa-reauth-dea-eap-master-session-key
; AVP: EAP-Master-Session-Key
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Command-Section: 4.2.2.1.2
; Section: 4.1.2.4.1
; Table: 4.1.2.4.1/4
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This IE shall be sent if Result-Code AVP is set to DIAMETER_SUCCESS."
    present-if Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: swa-reauth-dea-mps-priority
; AVP: MPS-Priority
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Command-Section: 4.2.2.1.2
; Section: 4.1.2.4.1
; Table: 4.1.2.4.1/4
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This information element shall be sent to the non-3GPP access network if the UE has an MPS subscription in the HSS."
    text-only


;; Clause 4.2.4, session handling: STa's, clause 5.2.4, whose
;; Auth-Session-State is never sent, in each SWa command.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: swa-der-4-2-2-1-1-no-auth-session-state
; AVP: Auth-Session-State
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Request
; Command-Section: 4.2.2.1.1
; Section: 4.2.4
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"The session handling for the SWa interface is the same as the STa session handling described in the clause 5.2.4."
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: swa-dea-4-2-2-1-2-no-auth-session-state
; AVP: Auth-Session-State
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Command-Section: 4.2.2.1.2
; Section: 4.2.4
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"The session handling for the SWa interface is the same as the STa session handling described in the clause 5.2.4."
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: swa-rar-4-2-2-4-1-no-auth-session-state
; AVP: Auth-Session-State
; Command: Re-Auth-Request
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 4.2.2.4.1
; Section: 4.2.4
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"The session handling for the SWa interface is the same as the STa session handling described in the clause 5.2.4."
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: swa-raa-4-2-2-4-2-no-auth-session-state
; AVP: Auth-Session-State
; Command: Re-Auth-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 4.2.2.4.2
; Section: 4.2.4
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"The session handling for the SWa interface is the same as the STa session handling described in the clause 5.2.4."
    absent


;; STa, clause 5: the tables of clause 5.1.2, describing the
;; Diameter-EAP-Request and -Answer of clause 5.2.2.1 and the AA-Request
;; and -Answer of clause 5.2.2.3 under 16777250. A condition naming the
;; Result-Code reads the answer's own; one on the request, the subscription
;; or what the AAA server decided stays text.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-der-auth-request-type
; AVP: Auth-Request-Type
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Request
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.1
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/1
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"AUTHORIZE_AUTHENTICATE shall be used in this case."
    range 3


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-der-mip6-feature-vector
; AVP: MIP6-Feature-Vector
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Request
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.1
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/1
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"The PMIP6_SUPPORTED flag and/or the GTPv2 SUPPORTED flag shall be set if the non-3GPP access supports PMIPv6 and/or GTPv2."
"The flag MIP6_INTEGRATED shall be set if DHCPv6 based Home Agent address discovery is supported as defined in IETF RFC 5447 [6]."
"The MIP4_SUPPORTED flag shall be set if the non-3GPP access supports MIPv4 FA-CoA mode."
    text-only


;; The TWAN inserts the Visited-Network-Identifier where its policy
;; has it (the row), and then the names. On SWd the 3GPP AAA Proxy
;; inserts the identifier into every request it forwards (clause
;; 6.1.2.1.1), where the names stay the access network's: SWd's row
;; is text-only.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-der-full-network-name
; AVP: Full-Network-Name
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Request
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.1
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/1
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"If the Visited Network Identifier is present, this AVP shall be set."
    present-if Visited-Network-Identifier


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-der-short-network-name
; AVP: Short-Network-Name
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Request
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.1
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/1
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"If the Visited Network Identifier is present, this AVP shall be set."
    present-if Visited-Network-Identifier


;; The command's body prints no Transport-Access-Type: the row describes an AVP the
;; ABNF carries only as *[ AVP ], so no scope names the command.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-der-transport-access-type
; AVP: Transport-Access-Type
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/1
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"if the access network needs to receive the IMSI of the UE in the authentication response, then this information element shall be present, and it shall contain the value \"BBF\" (see clause 5.2.3.19)."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-der-twan-connectivity-parameters
; AVP: TWAN-Connectivity-Parameters
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Request
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.1
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/1
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This information element shall be present if the 3GPP AAA Server has previously authorized the SCM to be used for EPC access."
"If the requested connectivity has been granted, the following information elements shall be included:"
    text-only


;; Provided connectivity parameters: a granted connectivity is one
;; with an address, the selected APN, PDN type and TWAG user-plane MAC
;; address beside it. The UE's requested parameters, sent in an answer,
;; hold no address. Which address the PDN type asks for, and the PCO
;; received from the PGW, no rule reads.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: twan-connectivity-parameters-granted-service-selection
; AVP: Service-Selection
; Within: TWAN-Connectivity-Parameters
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/1
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"If the requested connectivity has been granted, the following information elements shall be included:"
"The absence of both an IPv4 address and an IPv6 Interface Identifier indicates that the requested connectivity could not be granted."
    present-if Served-Party-IP-Address


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: twan-connectivity-parameters-granted-pdn-type
; AVP: PDN-Type
; Within: TWAN-Connectivity-Parameters
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/1
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"If the requested connectivity has been granted, the following information elements shall be included:"
"The absence of both an IPv4 address and an IPv6 Interface Identifier indicates that the requested connectivity could not be granted."
    present-if Served-Party-IP-Address


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: twan-connectivity-parameters-granted-twag-up-address
; AVP: TWAG-UP-Address
; Within: TWAN-Connectivity-Parameters
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/1
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"If the requested connectivity has been granted, the following information elements shall be included:"
"The absence of both an IPv4 address and an IPv6 Interface Identifier indicates that the requested connectivity could not be granted."
    present-if Served-Party-IP-Address


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-der-twag-cp-address
; AVP: TWAG-CP-Address
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Request
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.1
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/1
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"The TWAN shall include this IE if it indicates support of the MCM in the Supported TWAN Connection Modes IE."
    present-if TWAN-Connection-Mode bit MC-MODE


;; The command's body prints no IMEI-Check-In-VPLMN-Result: the row describes an AVP the
;; ABNF carries only as *[ AVP ], so no scope names the command.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-der-imei-check-in-vplmn-result
; AVP: IMEI-Check-In-VPLMN-Result
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/1
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"The 3GPP AAA Proxy shall include this IE if it has performed an IMEI check in the VPLMN."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-der-high-priority-access-info
; AVP: High-Priority-Access-Info
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Request
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.1
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/1
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"Based on operator policy, this information element shall be sent to the 3GPP AAA Server if the UE has access priority conveyed in an EAP response/identity message"
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-dea-auth-request-type
; AVP: Auth-Request-Type
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"It shall contain the value AUTHORIZE_AUTHENTICATE."
    range 3


;; The answer authorizing the SCM after a correct EAP-AKA' response
;; sets DEA-Flags' TWAN-S2a-Connectivity-Indicator with
;; DIAMETER_MULTI_ROUND_AUTH and leaves EAP-Payload out (clause
;; 5.1.2.1.2); an EAP round's DIAMETER_MULTI_ROUND_AUTH sets no such bit.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-dea-eap-payload
; AVP: EAP-Payload
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This IE shall not be included if the UE has been authenticated and the 3GPP AAA Server authorizes the SCM for EPC access for the UE and the Result-Code AVP is set to DIAMETER_MULTI_ROUND_AUTH."
    absent-if Result-Code = DIAMETER_MULTI_ROUND_AUTH and DEA-Flags bit TWAN-S2a-Connectivity-Indicator


;; The answer of the first exchange: a row allowed with DIAMETER_SUCCESS
;; or with DIAMETER_MULTI_ROUND_AUTH and DEA-Flags' TWAN-S2a-Connectivity-
;; Indicator reads both; what was authorized is not read. An ERP
;; re-authentication's success, whose request sets DER-Flags'
;; ERP-Re-Authentication, shares the print and carries its rMSK in Key
;; (table 5.1.2.5.1/2), no EAP-Master-Session-Key.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-dea-eap-master-session-key
; AVP: EAP-Master-Session-Key
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Request-Section: 5.2.2.1.1
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This IE shall be present if Result-Code AVP is set to DIAMETER_SUCCESS."
    present-if Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS and not request/DER-Flags bit ERP-Re-Authentication


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-dea-context-identifier
; AVP: Context-Identifier
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"It shall only be included if NBM is authorized for use, the non-3GPP access network was decided to be trusted, the Emergency-Indication bit of the Emergency-Services AVP is not set in the Authentication and Authorization Answer and the Result-Code AVP is set to either: - DIAMETER_SUCCESS or - DIAMETER_MULTI_ROUND_AUTH, and TWAN-S2a-Connectivity-Indicator is set in DEA-Flags."
    requires Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS or Result-Code = DIAMETER_MULTI_ROUND_AUTH and DEA-Flags bit TWAN-S2a-Connectivity-Indicator
    absent-if Emergency-Services bit Emergency-Indication


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-dea-apn-oi-replacement
; AVP: APN-OI-Replacement
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"It shall only be included if NBM is authorized for use, the Emergency-Indication bit of the Emergency-Services AVP is not set in the Authentication and Authorization Answer and the Result-Code AVP is set to either: - DIAMETER_SUCCESS or - DIAMETER_MULTI_ROUND_AUTH, and TWAN-S2a-Connectivity-Indicator is set in DEA-Flags."
    requires Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS or Result-Code = DIAMETER_MULTI_ROUND_AUTH and DEA-Flags bit TWAN-S2a-Connectivity-Indicator
    absent-if Emergency-Services bit Emergency-Indication


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-dea-apn-configuration
; AVP: APN-Configuration
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This information element shall only be sent if EPC Access is authorized, the Emergency-Indication bit of the Emergency-Services AVP is not set in the Authentication and Authorization Answer and the Result-Code AVP is set to either: - DIAMETER_SUCCESS or - DIAMETER_MULTI_ROUND_AUTH, and TWAN-S2a-Connectivity-Indicator is set in DEA-Flags."
    requires Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS or Result-Code = DIAMETER_MULTI_ROUND_AUTH and DEA-Flags bit TWAN-S2a-Connectivity-Indicator
    absent-if Emergency-Services bit Emergency-Indication


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-dea-mip6-feature-vector
; AVP: MIP6-Feature-Vector
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This information element shall only be sent if EPC Access is authorized and if the Result-Code AVP is set to either: - DIAMETER_SUCCESS or - DIAMETER_MULTI_ROUND_AUTH, and TWAN-S2a-Connectivity-Indicator is set in DEA-Flags."
    requires Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS or Result-Code = DIAMETER_MULTI_ROUND_AUTH and DEA-Flags bit TWAN-S2a-Connectivity-Indicator


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-dea-mobile-node-identifier
; AVP: Mobile-Node-Identifier
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This information element shall only be sent if the Result-Code AVP is set to either: - DIAMETER_SUCCESS or - DIAMETER_MULTI_ROUND_AUTH, and TWAN-S2a-Connectivity-Indicator is set in DEA-Flags."
    requires Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS or Result-Code = DIAMETER_MULTI_ROUND_AUTH and DEA-Flags bit TWAN-S2a-Connectivity-Indicator
"If this IE contains an identity based on IMSI, this IE shall not include the leading digit prepended in front of the IMSI used to differentiate between authentication schemes."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-dea-redirect-host
; AVP: Redirect-Host
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This information element shall be sent if the Result-Code value is set to DIAMETER_REDIRECT_INDICATION."
    present-if Result-Code = DIAMETER_REDIRECT_INDICATION


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-dea-ambr
; AVP: AMBR
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"It shall be present only if the non-3GPP access network was decided to be trusted, the Result-Code AVP is set to DIAMETER_SUCCESS and ANID is \"HRPD\"."
    requires Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS


;; The first exchange is SWa's and STa's (clause 4.2.1), and a
;; decision for an untrusted access is sent in it under STa's
;; 16777250, whose prints are STa's and SWd's: no message shows the
;; STa case apart from the value.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-dea-an-trusted
; AVP: AN-Trusted
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This AVP shall be included only in the first authentication and authorization response."
    text-only
"For the STa case, the value \"TRUSTED\" shall be used."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-dea-mip-fa-rk
; AVP: MIP-FA-RK
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This AVP shall be present if MIPv4 FACoA mode is used, the MN-FA authentication extension is supported and the Result-Code AVP is set to DIAMETER_SUCCESS."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-dea-mip-fa-rk-spi
; AVP: MIP-FA-RK-SPI
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This AVP shall be present if MIP-FA-RK is present"
    present-if MIP-FA-RK


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-dea-trace-info
; AVP: Trace-Info
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This information element shall only be sent if the Result-Code AVP is set to either: - DIAMETER_SUCCESS or - DIAMETER_MULTI_ROUND_AUTH, and TWAN-S2a-Connectivity-Indicator is set in DEA-Flags."
    requires Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS or Result-Code = DIAMETER_MULTI_ROUND_AUTH and DEA-Flags bit TWAN-S2a-Connectivity-Indicator
"This AVP shall be included if the subscriber and equipment trace has been activated for the user in the HSS and signalling based activation is used to download the trace activation from the HSS to the non-3GPP access network."
    text-only
"Only the Trace-Data AVP shall be included to the Trace-Info AVP"
    members only Trace-Data


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-dea-subscription-id
; AVP: Subscription-Id
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This AVP shall contain the MSISDN of the UE and shall be sent if it is available and the non-3GPP access network is trusted and the Result-Code AVP is set to either: - DIAMETER_SUCCESS or - DIAMETER_MULTI_ROUND_AUTH, and TWAN-S2a-Connectivity-Indicator is set in DEA-Flags."
    requires Subscription-Id/Subscription-Id-Type = END_USER_E164


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-dea-twan-connection-mode
; AVP: TWAN-Connection-Mode
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"The 3GPP AAA Server shall include this IE if it selects either the SCM or MCM and the Result-Code AVP is set to either: - DIAMETER_SUCCESS or - DIAMETER_MULTI_ROUND_AUTH, and TWAN-S2a-Connectivity-Indicator is set in DEA-Flags."
"If this IE is not present, the TWAN shall use TSCM."
    text-only
"When present, this IE shall indicate the selected mode of operation (either SCM or MCM)."
    bits only 1 2
    bits at-least-one 1 2
    bits at-most-one 1 2


;; The attach type is Connectivity-Flags' Initial-Attach-Indicator
;; (clause 5.2.3.27), the requested PDN type PDN-Type.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-dea-twan-connectivity-parameters
; AVP: TWAN-Connectivity-Parameters
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This IE shall contain the requested connectivity parameters received from the UE if the 3GPP AAA Server authorizes the SCM for TWAN and the Result-Code AVP is set to DIAMETER_MULTI_ROUND_AUTH, and TWAN-S2a-Connectivity-Indicator is set in DEA-Flags."
    text-only
"When present, the following information elements shall be included: - attach type (initial attach or handover)"
    members at-least-one Connectivity-Flags
    members at-least-one PDN-Type


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-dea-wlcp-key
; AVP: WLCP-Key
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This IE shall be present if the Result-Code AVP is set to DIAMETER_SUCCESS and the selected TWAN Connection Mode is MCM."
    present-if Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS and TWAN-Connection-Mode bit MC-MODE


;; IMEI is a member of TS 29.272's Terminal-Information, which this file
;; re-uses: a members rule names it as the defining document prints it.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-dea-terminal-information
; AVP: Terminal-Information
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"For a trusted WLAN access, the 3GPP AAA Server shall include this IE if the user's Mobile Equipment Identity is available."
    text-only
"When present, this grouped AVP shall contain the IMEI AVP and, if available, the Software Version AVP."
    members at-least-one IMEI


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-dea-emergency-services
; AVP: Emergency-Services
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"it shall include this IE and set the Emergency-Indication bit when the UE indicates an Emergency Attach in EAP-AKA' signalling."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-dea-emergency-info
; AVP: Emergency-Info
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"It shall be present for a non-roaming authenticated user, if this information was received from the HSS, the TWAN indicated support of IMS Emergency sessions and the Result-Code AVP is set to either: - DIAMETER_SUCCESS or - DIAMETER_MULTI_ROUND_AUTH and TWAN-S2a-Connectivity-Indicator is set in DEA-Flags."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-dea-key
; AVP: Key
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"If the 3GPP AAA Server supports ERP, this IE shall be present if the Result-Code AVP is set to DIAMETER_SUCCESS, the domain-specific re-authentication key was requested and the use of ERP is authorized for this user (see clause 8.2.3.27)."
    text-only


;; The ERP Keying Material of the first exchange: an ERP
;; re-authentication's success, sharing the print, carries its rMSK in
;; Key and neither EAP-Master-Session-Key nor ERP-Realm (table
;; 5.1.2.5.1/2).
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-dea-erp-realm
; AVP: ERP-Realm
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This IE shall be present if the ERP Keying Material is present."
    present-if Key and EAP-Master-Session-Key


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-dea-ue-usage-type
; AVP: UE-Usage-Type
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This IE shall be present if this information is available in the user subscription."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-dea-mps-priority
; AVP: MPS-Priority
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"Based on operator policy, this information element shall be sent to the non-3GPP WLAN access if the UE has an MPS subscription in the HSS."
    text-only


;; And table 5.1.2.1/1's of SWd's print of the request.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: swd-der-auth-request-type
; AVP: Auth-Request-Type
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Request
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 6.2.2.1.1.1
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/1
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"AUTHORIZE_AUTHENTICATE shall be used in this case."
    range 3


;; SWd carries STa's first exchange, the 3GPP AAA Proxy forwarding it
;; (clause 6.1.2.1.1): table 5.1.2.1/2's rows hold of SWd's print of
;; the answer, which a message under 16777250 may be held to in STa's
;; place.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: swd-dea-auth-request-type
; AVP: Auth-Request-Type
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 6.2.2.1.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"It shall contain the value AUTHORIZE_AUTHENTICATE."
    range 3


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: swd-dea-eap-payload
; AVP: EAP-Payload
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 6.2.2.1.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This IE shall not be included if the UE has been authenticated and the 3GPP AAA Server authorizes the SCM for EPC access for the UE and the Result-Code AVP is set to DIAMETER_MULTI_ROUND_AUTH."
    absent-if Result-Code = DIAMETER_MULTI_ROUND_AUTH and DEA-Flags bit TWAN-S2a-Connectivity-Indicator


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: swd-dea-eap-master-session-key
; AVP: EAP-Master-Session-Key
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 6.2.2.1.1.2
; Request-Section: 6.2.2.1.1.1
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This IE shall be present if Result-Code AVP is set to DIAMETER_SUCCESS."
    present-if Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS and not request/DER-Flags bit ERP-Re-Authentication


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: swd-dea-context-identifier
; AVP: Context-Identifier
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 6.2.2.1.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"It shall only be included if NBM is authorized for use, the non-3GPP access network was decided to be trusted, the Emergency-Indication bit of the Emergency-Services AVP is not set in the Authentication and Authorization Answer and the Result-Code AVP is set to either: - DIAMETER_SUCCESS or - DIAMETER_MULTI_ROUND_AUTH, and TWAN-S2a-Connectivity-Indicator is set in DEA-Flags."
    requires Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS or Result-Code = DIAMETER_MULTI_ROUND_AUTH and DEA-Flags bit TWAN-S2a-Connectivity-Indicator
    absent-if Emergency-Services bit Emergency-Indication


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: swd-dea-apn-oi-replacement
; AVP: APN-OI-Replacement
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 6.2.2.1.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"It shall only be included if NBM is authorized for use, the Emergency-Indication bit of the Emergency-Services AVP is not set in the Authentication and Authorization Answer and the Result-Code AVP is set to either: - DIAMETER_SUCCESS or - DIAMETER_MULTI_ROUND_AUTH, and TWAN-S2a-Connectivity-Indicator is set in DEA-Flags."
    requires Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS or Result-Code = DIAMETER_MULTI_ROUND_AUTH and DEA-Flags bit TWAN-S2a-Connectivity-Indicator
    absent-if Emergency-Services bit Emergency-Indication


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: swd-dea-apn-configuration
; AVP: APN-Configuration
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 6.2.2.1.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This information element shall only be sent if EPC Access is authorized, the Emergency-Indication bit of the Emergency-Services AVP is not set in the Authentication and Authorization Answer and the Result-Code AVP is set to either: - DIAMETER_SUCCESS or - DIAMETER_MULTI_ROUND_AUTH, and TWAN-S2a-Connectivity-Indicator is set in DEA-Flags."
    requires Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS or Result-Code = DIAMETER_MULTI_ROUND_AUTH and DEA-Flags bit TWAN-S2a-Connectivity-Indicator
    absent-if Emergency-Services bit Emergency-Indication


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: swd-dea-mip6-feature-vector
; AVP: MIP6-Feature-Vector
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 6.2.2.1.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This information element shall only be sent if EPC Access is authorized and if the Result-Code AVP is set to either: - DIAMETER_SUCCESS or - DIAMETER_MULTI_ROUND_AUTH, and TWAN-S2a-Connectivity-Indicator is set in DEA-Flags."
    requires Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS or Result-Code = DIAMETER_MULTI_ROUND_AUTH and DEA-Flags bit TWAN-S2a-Connectivity-Indicator


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: swd-dea-mobile-node-identifier
; AVP: Mobile-Node-Identifier
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 6.2.2.1.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This information element shall only be sent if the Result-Code AVP is set to either: - DIAMETER_SUCCESS or - DIAMETER_MULTI_ROUND_AUTH, and TWAN-S2a-Connectivity-Indicator is set in DEA-Flags."
    requires Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS or Result-Code = DIAMETER_MULTI_ROUND_AUTH and DEA-Flags bit TWAN-S2a-Connectivity-Indicator


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: swd-dea-redirect-host
; AVP: Redirect-Host
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 6.2.2.1.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This information element shall be sent if the Result-Code value is set to DIAMETER_REDIRECT_INDICATION."
    present-if Result-Code = DIAMETER_REDIRECT_INDICATION


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: swd-dea-mip-fa-rk-spi
; AVP: MIP-FA-RK-SPI
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 6.2.2.1.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This AVP shall be present if MIP-FA-RK is present"
    present-if MIP-FA-RK


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: swd-dea-trace-info
; AVP: Trace-Info
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 6.2.2.1.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This information element shall only be sent if the Result-Code AVP is set to either: - DIAMETER_SUCCESS or - DIAMETER_MULTI_ROUND_AUTH, and TWAN-S2a-Connectivity-Indicator is set in DEA-Flags."
    requires Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS or Result-Code = DIAMETER_MULTI_ROUND_AUTH and DEA-Flags bit TWAN-S2a-Connectivity-Indicator
"Only the Trace-Data AVP shall be included to the Trace-Info AVP"
    members only Trace-Data


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: swd-dea-subscription-id
; AVP: Subscription-Id
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 6.2.2.1.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This AVP shall contain the MSISDN of the UE and shall be sent if it is available and the non-3GPP access network is trusted and the Result-Code AVP is set to either: - DIAMETER_SUCCESS or - DIAMETER_MULTI_ROUND_AUTH, and TWAN-S2a-Connectivity-Indicator is set in DEA-Flags."
    requires Subscription-Id/Subscription-Id-Type = END_USER_E164


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: swd-dea-twan-connection-mode
; AVP: TWAN-Connection-Mode
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 6.2.2.1.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"When present, this IE shall indicate the selected mode of operation (either SCM or MCM)."
    bits only 1 2
    bits at-least-one 1 2
    bits at-most-one 1 2


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: swd-dea-twan-connectivity-parameters
; AVP: TWAN-Connectivity-Parameters
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 6.2.2.1.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"When present, the following information elements shall be included: - attach type (initial attach or handover)"
    members at-least-one Connectivity-Flags
    members at-least-one PDN-Type


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: swd-dea-wlcp-key
; AVP: WLCP-Key
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 6.2.2.1.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This IE shall be present if the Result-Code AVP is set to DIAMETER_SUCCESS and the selected TWAN Connection Mode is MCM."
    present-if Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS and TWAN-Connection-Mode bit MC-MODE


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: swd-dea-terminal-information
; AVP: Terminal-Information
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 6.2.2.1.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"When present, this grouped AVP shall contain the IMEI AVP and, if available, the Software Version AVP."
    members at-least-one IMEI


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: swd-dea-erp-realm
; AVP: ERP-Realm
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 6.2.2.1.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.1.1
; Table: 5.1.2.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This IE shall be present if the ERP Keying Material is present."
    present-if Key and EAP-Master-Session-Key


;; AUTHORIZE_ONLY is 2 (IETF RFC 6733 clause 8.7).
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-aar-auth-request-type
; AVP: Auth-Request-Type
; Command: AA-Request
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Section: 5.1.2.3.1
; Table: 5.1.2.3.1/3
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"In this case, it shall have the value: AUTHORIZE_ONLY"
    range 2


;; Re-authorization over AA-Request and -Answer, and re-authentication
;; over the Diameter-EAP-Request and -Answer the first exchange uses.
;; Clause 5.2.3.3 lists the flags in prose, which the file holds as no
;; bit table: a bits rule names only bits a table holds.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-aar-mip6-feature-vector
; AVP: MIP6-Feature-Vector
; Command: AA-Request
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Section: 5.1.2.3.1
; Table: 5.1.2.3.1/3
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This AVP shall be included only if optimized idle mode mobility from E-UTRAN to HRPD access is executed."
    text-only
"When included, the PMIP_SUPPORTED and the OPTIMIZED_IDLE_MODE_MOBILITY flags shall be set."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-aar-high-priority-access-info
; AVP: High-Priority-Access-Info
; Command: AA-Request
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Section: 5.1.2.3.1
; Table: 5.1.2.3.1/3
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"Based on operator policy, this information element shall be sent to the 3GPP AAA Server if the UE has access priority"
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-aaa-auth-request-type
; AVP: Auth-Request-Type
; Command: AA-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Section: 5.1.2.3.1
; Table: 5.1.2.3.1/4
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"It shall contain the value AUTHORIZE_ONLY."
    range 2


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-aaa-context-identifier
; AVP: Context-Identifier
; Command: AA-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Section: 5.1.2.3.1
; Table: 5.1.2.3.1/4
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"It shall only be included if NBM is authorized for use, the Emergency-Indication AVP was not present in the initial Authentication and Authorization Answer and the Result-Code AVP is set to DIAMETER_SUCCESS."
    requires Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-aaa-apn-oi-replacement
; AVP: APN-OI-Replacement
; Command: AA-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Section: 5.1.2.3.1
; Table: 5.1.2.3.1/4
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"It shall only be included if NBM is authorized for use, the Emergency-Indication bit of the Emergency-Services AVP was not set in the initial Authentication and Authorization Answer and the Result-Code AVP is set to DIAMETER_SUCCESS."
    requires Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-aaa-apn-configuration
; AVP: APN-Configuration
; Command: AA-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Section: 5.1.2.3.1
; Table: 5.1.2.3.1/4
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This information element shall only be sent if the Emergency-Indication bit of the Emergency-Services AVP was not set in the initial Authentication and Authorization Answer and the Result-Code AVP is set to DIAMETER_SUCCESS."
    requires Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS


;; The command's body prints no AMBR: the row describes an AVP the
;; ABNF carries only as *[ AVP ], so no scope names the command.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-aaa-ambr
; AVP: AMBR
; Section: 5.1.2.3.1
; Table: 5.1.2.3.1/4
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"It shall be present if the Result-Code AVP is set to DIAMETER_SUCCESS and ANID is \"HRPD\"."
    text-only


;; The command's body admits MIP6-Feature-Vector only through * [ AVP ],
;; which makes it a member there. Clause 5.2.3.3 lists the flags in prose,
;; which the file holds as no bit table: a bits rule names only bits a
;; table holds.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-aaa-mip6-feature-vector
; AVP: MIP6-Feature-Vector
; Command: AA-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.3.4
; Section: 5.1.2.3.1
; Table: 5.1.2.3.1/4
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This information element shall only be sent if it has been received in the corresponding authorization request and the Result-Code AVP is set to DIAMETER_SUCCESS."
    requires request/MIP6-Feature-Vector and Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS
"When included, the PMIP_SUPPORTED and the OPTIMIZED_IDLE_MODE_MOBILITY flags shall be set."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-aaa-trace-info
; AVP: Trace-Info
; Command: AA-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Section: 5.1.2.3.1
; Table: 5.1.2.3.1/4
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This AVP shall be included if the subscriber and equipment trace has been activated for the user in the HSS and signalling based activation is used to download the trace activation from the HSS to the trusted non-3GPP access network."
    text-only
"Only the Trace-Data AVP shall be included to the Trace-Info AVP"
    members only Trace-Data


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-aaa-subscription-id
; AVP: Subscription-Id
; Command: AA-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Section: 5.1.2.3.1
; Table: 5.1.2.3.1/4
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This AVP shall contain the MSISDN of the UE and shall be sent if it is available and the Result-Code AVP is set to DIAMETER_SUCCESS."
    requires Subscription-Id/Subscription-Id-Type = END_USER_E164


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-aaa-emergency-info
; AVP: Emergency-Info
; Command: AA-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Section: 5.1.2.3.1
; Table: 5.1.2.3.1/4
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"It shall be present for a non-roaming authenticated user, if this information was received from the HSS, the TWAN indicated support of IMS Emergency Sessions and the Result-Code AVP is set to DIAMETER_SUCCESS."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-aaa-ue-usage-type
; AVP: UE-Usage-Type
; Command: AA-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Section: 5.1.2.3.1
; Table: 5.1.2.3.1/4
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This IE shall be present if this information is available in the user subscription."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-aaa-mps-priority
; AVP: MPS-Priority
; Command: AA-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Section: 5.1.2.3.1
; Table: 5.1.2.3.1/4
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"Based on operator policy, this information element shall be sent to the non-3GPP WLAN access if the UE has an MPS subscription in the HSS."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-reauth-der-high-priority-access-info
; AVP: High-Priority-Access-Info
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Request
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.1
; Section: 5.1.2.3.1
; Table: 5.1.2.3.1/5
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"Based on operator policy, this information element shall be sent to the 3GPP AAA Server if the UE has access priority"
    text-only


;; A re-authentication's answer is the first exchange's Diameter-EAP-Answer:
;; a row allowing DIAMETER_SUCCESS alone, where the first allows
;; DIAMETER_MULTI_ROUND_AUTH too, would refuse the first exchange's answer,
;; and stays text.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-reauth-dea-eap-master-session-key
; AVP: EAP-Master-Session-Key
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Request-Section: 5.2.2.1.1
; Section: 5.1.2.3.1
; Table: 5.1.2.3.1/6
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This IE shall be sent if Result-Code AVP is set to DIAMETER_SUCCESS."
    present-if Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS and not request/DER-Flags bit ERP-Re-Authentication


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-reauth-dea-context-identifier
; AVP: Context-Identifier
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.3.1
; Table: 5.1.2.3.1/6
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"It shall only be included if NBM is authorized for use, the Emergency-Indication bit of the Emergency-Services AVP was not set in the initial Authentication and Authorization Answer and the Result-Code AVP is set to DIAMETER_SUCCESS."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-reauth-dea-apn-oi-replacement
; AVP: APN-OI-Replacement
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.3.1
; Table: 5.1.2.3.1/6
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"It shall only be included if NBM is authorized for use, the Emergency-Indication bit of the Emergency-Services AVP was not set in the initial Authentication and Authorization Answer and the Result-Code AVP is set to DIAMETER_SUCCESS."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-reauth-dea-apn-configuration
; AVP: APN-Configuration
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.3.1
; Table: 5.1.2.3.1/6
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This information element shall only be sent if the non-3GPP access network was decided to be trusted, the Emergency-Indication bit of the Emergency-Services AVP was not set in the initial Authentication and Authorization Answer and the Result-Code AVP is set to DIAMETER_SUCCESS."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-reauth-dea-ambr
; AVP: AMBR
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.3.1
; Table: 5.1.2.3.1/6
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"It shall be present only if the non-3GPP access network was decided to be trusted, the Result-Code AVP is set to DIAMETER_SUCCESS and ANID is \"HRPD\"."
    requires Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-reauth-dea-mip-fa-rk
; AVP: MIP-FA-RK
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.3.1
; Table: 5.1.2.3.1/6
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This AVP shall be present if MIPv4 is used, MN-FA authentication extension is supported and the Result-Code AVP is set to DIAMETER_SUCCESS."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-reauth-dea-mip-fa-rk-spi
; AVP: MIP-FA-RK-SPI
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.3.1
; Table: 5.1.2.3.1/6
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This AVP shall be present if MIP-FA-RK is present"
    present-if MIP-FA-RK


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-reauth-dea-trace-info
; AVP: Trace-Info
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.3.1
; Table: 5.1.2.3.1/6
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This AVP shall be included if the subscriber and equipment trace has been activated for the user in the HSS and signalling based activation is used to download the trace activation from the HSS to the trusted non-3GPP access network."
    text-only
"Only the Trace-Data AVP shall be included to the Trace-Info AVP"
    members only Trace-Data


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-reauth-dea-subscription-id
; AVP: Subscription-Id
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.3.1
; Table: 5.1.2.3.1/6
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This AVP shall contain the MSISDN of the UE and shall be sent if it is available and the Result-Code AVP is set to DIAMETER_SUCCESS."
    requires Subscription-Id/Subscription-Id-Type = END_USER_E164


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-reauth-dea-wlcp-key
; AVP: WLCP-Key
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.3.1
; Table: 5.1.2.3.1/6
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This IE shall be present if the Result-Code AVP is set to DIAMETER_SUCCESS and the TWAN Connection Mode previously selected is MCM."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-reauth-dea-emergency-info
; AVP: Emergency-Info
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.3.1
; Table: 5.1.2.3.1/6
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"It shall be present for a non-roaming authenticated user, if this information was received from the HSS, the TWAN indicated support of IMS Emergency Sessions and the Result-Code AVP is set to DIAMETER_SUCCESS."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-reauth-dea-ue-usage-type
; AVP: UE-Usage-Type
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.3.1
; Table: 5.1.2.3.1/6
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This IE shall be present if this information is available in the user subscription."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-reauth-dea-mps-priority
; AVP: MPS-Priority
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Section: 5.1.2.3.1
; Table: 5.1.2.3.1/6
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"Based on operator policy, this information element shall be sent to the non-3GPP access network if the UE has an MPS subscription in the HSS."
    text-only


;; The answer to an ERP re-authentication is the first exchange's
;; Diameter-EAP-Answer, its request's DER-Flags setting
;; ERP-Re-Authentication (clause 5.2.3.20); clause 5.1.2.5.2 answers a
;; successful one with DIAMETER_SUCCESS.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-erp-dea-key
; AVP: Key
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.2
; Request-Section: 5.2.2.1.1
; Section: 5.1.2.5.1
; Table: 5.1.2.5.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"This IE shall be present if the ERP re-authentication is successful."
    present-if Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS and request/DER-Flags bit ERP-Re-Authentication


;; The AVP clauses of 5.2.3.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: service-selection-labels
; AVP: Service-Selection
; Section: 5.2.3.5
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"The contents of the Service-Selection AVP shall be formatted as a character string composed of one or more labels separated by dots (\".\")."
    encoding labels


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: anid-element
; AVP: ANID
; Section: 5.2.3.7
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"The ANID AVP is of type UTF8String; this AVP contains the Access Network Identity; see"
    encoding element TS24.302 8.1.1 "Access Network Identity"


;; Each application of the document sets it to 1 in a clause of its own
;; (7.2.3.2, 8.2.3.15, 9.2.3.4), each read in its application's messages. A
;; feature list is named by the application, the Vendor-Id and the
;; Feature-List-ID (TS 29.229 clause 6.3.29), so the value is the 3GPP
;; list's: another vendor's lists take their own numbers.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-feature-list-id
; AVP: Feature-List-ID
; Within: Supported-Features
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Section: 5.2.3.10
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"For this release, the Feature-List-ID AVP value shall be set to 1 for the STa/SWa application."
    values 1 if Vendor-Id = 10415


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: mip-fa-rk-element
; AVP: MIP-FA-RK
; Section: 5.2.3.12
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"The MIP-FA-RK AVP is of type OctetString; this AVP contains the FA-RK used to calculate the security parameters needed for the MN-FA authentication extension as defined by"
    encoding element TS33.402 9.2.1.2.2 "FA-RK"


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: mip-fa-rk-spi-element
; AVP: MIP-FA-RK-SPI
; Section: 5.2.3.13
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"The MIP-FA-RK-SPI AVP is of type Unsigned32; this AVP contains the security index used in identifying the security context for the FA-RK as defined by"
    encoding element TS33.402 9.2.1.2.2 "FA-RK-SPI"


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: full-network-name-element
; AVP: Full-Network-Name
; Section: 5.2.3.14
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"The Full-Network-Name AVP is of type OctetString; this AVP shall contain the Full Network Name and be encoded as the Full name value field of the AT_FULL_NAME_FOR_NETWORK attribute specified in clause 8.2.5.1"
    encoding element TS24.302 8.2.5.1 "Full name value"


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: short-network-name-element
; AVP: Short-Network-Name
; Section: 5.2.3.15
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"The Short-Network-Name AVP is of type OctetString; this AVP shall contain the Short Network Name and be encoded as the Short name value field of the AT_SHORT_NAME_FOR_NETWORK attribute specified in clause 8.2.5.2"
    encoding element TS24.302 8.2.5.2 "Short name value"


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: der-flags-undefined-bits
; AVP: DER-Flags
; Section: 5.2.3.20
; Table: 5.2.3.20/1
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"NOTE: Bits not defined in this table shall be cleared by the sender and discarded by the receiver of the command."
    bits only 0 1 2 3 4 5 6


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: dea-flags-undefined-bits
; AVP: DEA-Flags
; Section: 5.2.3.21
; Table: 5.2.3.21/1
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"NOTE: Bits not defined in this table shall be cleared by the sender and discarded by the recever of the command."
    bits only 0 1 2


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ssid-length
; AVP: SSID
; Section: 5.2.3.22
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"It shall contain a string of 1 to 32 octets."
    length 1..32 octets


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: hessid-mac-address
; AVP: HESSID
; Section: 5.2.3.23
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"The HESSID AVP is of type UTF8String and it shall contain a 6-octet MAC address that identifies the Homogenous Extended Service Set (see IEEE Std 802.11-2012 [40]). It shall be encoded in upper-case ASCII characters with the octet values separated by dash characters. It shall contain a string of 17 octets."
    encoding mac-address
    length 17 octets


;; The AVP describes a WLAN, trusted or untrusted, so the SSID is always
;; there; which further element the operator's policy leaves to it.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: access-network-info-ssid
; AVP: Access-Network-Info
; Section: 5.2.3.24
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"For a Trusted WLAN, it shall contain the SSID of the WLAN and, unless otherwise determined by the TWAN operator's policies, it shall contain at least one of the following elements:"
"For an untrusted WLAN, it shall contain the same information as specified above for a trusted WLAN, where the operator name indicates the WLAN operator name."
    members at-least-one SSID


;; The Code field is the payload's third octet, which no rule kind reads
;; in a payload of any length; so is Operator-Name's Namespace ID below,
;; its first.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: access-network-info-location-information
; AVP: Location-Information
; Within: Access-Network-Info
; Section: 5.2.3.24
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"the content of Location-Information shall indicate that the encoding follows a civic location profile, by setting the \"Code\" field to 0."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: access-network-info-operator-name
; AVP: Operator-Name
; Within: Access-Network-Info
; Section: 5.2.3.24
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"Only values \"1\" (Realm) and \"2\" (E212, containing MCC and MNC values) shall be used in this specification."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: twan-connection-mode-undefined-bits
; AVP: TWAN-Connection-Mode
; Section: 5.2.3.25
; Table: 5.2.3.25/1
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"NOTE: Bits not defined in this table shall be cleared by the sender and discarded by the receiver of the command."
    bits only 0 1 2


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: twan-connectivity-parameters-service-selection
; AVP: Service-Selection
; Within: TWAN-Connectivity-Parameters
; Section: 5.2.3.26
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"It shall contain both the network identifier part and the operator identifier part of the Access Point Name."
    text-only


;; IPv4 (0), IPv6 (1) and IPv4v6 (2) of TS 29.272 clause 7.3.62, not its
;; IPv4_OR_IPv6 (3), a subscription's.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: twan-connectivity-parameters-pdn-type
; AVP: PDN-Type
; Within: TWAN-Connectivity-Parameters
; Section: 5.2.3.26
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"It may be set to IPv4, IPv6 or IPv4v6."
    range 0..2


;; An IPv4 address or an IPv6 interface identifier, each an Address:
;; whether the connection was established is the TWAN's, and that an
;; IPv6 one's upper 64 bits are zero no codec of a family reads.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: twan-connectivity-parameters-served-party-ip-address
; AVP: Served-Party-IP-Address
; Within: TWAN-Connectivity-Parameters
; Section: 5.2.3.26
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"These AVPs shall be present if the S2a connection was successfully established, and they shall contain either of:"
    encoding ip-address
"For the IPv6 interface identifier, the higher 64 bits of the address shall be set to zero."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: connectivity-flags-undefined-bits
; AVP: Connectivity-Flags
; Section: 5.2.3.27
; Table: 5.2.3.26/1
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"NOTE: Bits not defined in this table shall be cleared by the sender and discarded by the receiver of the command."
    bits only 0


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: twag-cp-address-ip
; AVP: TWAG-CP-Address
; Section: 5.2.3.29
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"The TWAG-CP-Address AVP is of type Address and shall contain the TWAG control-plane IPv4 and/or IPv6 address that the TWAG supports, to be used for WLCP by the UE if MCM is selected."
    encoding ip-address


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: twag-up-address-mac-address
; AVP: TWAG-UP-Address
; Section: 5.2.3.30
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"The TWAG-UP-Address AVP is of type UTF8String and shall contain a 6-octet MAC address that identifies the TWAG user-plane MAC address to be used for encapsulating user plane packets between the UE and the TWAN, when SCM is used."
"It shall be encoded in upper-case ASCII characters with the octet values separated by dash characters. It shall contain a string of 17 octets."
    encoding mac-address
    length 17 octets


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: wlcp-key-element
; AVP: WLCP-Key
; Section: 5.2.3.33
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"The WLCP-Key AVP (AVP Code 1535) is of type OctetString and it shall contain the WLCP Key used for protecting the WLCP signalling between the UE and the TWAN, as specified in"
    encoding element TS33.402 A.3 "WLCP key"


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: high-priority-access-info-undefined-bits
; AVP: High-Priority-Access-Info
; Section: 5.2.3.36
; Table: 5.2.3.36/1
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"NOTE: Bits not defined in this table shall be cleared by the sending TWAN and discarded by the receiving AAA Server."
    bits only 0


;; Clause 5.2.4, session handling: every command of the interface but
;; the ASR, whose Auth-Session-State a 3GPP AAA Proxy may override
;; (clauses 5.1.2.2.3, 7.1.2.4.3, 9.1.2.4.4), each admitting the AVP
;; through its * [ AVP ].
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-der-5-2-2-1-1-no-auth-session-state
; AVP: Auth-Session-State
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Request
; Application-ID: 16777250
; Command-Section: 5.2.2.1.1
; Section: 5.2.4
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"In order to indicate that the session state is to be maintained, the Diameter client and server shall not include the Auth-Session-State AVP, either in the request or in the response messages"
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-dea-5-2-2-1-2-no-auth-session-state
; AVP: Auth-Session-State
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777250
