;; Clause 10.3.1, of every answer: none of the clause's codes in
;; Result-Code but those IETF RFC 6733 numbers too (5001, 5003, 5004,
;; 5005); and, where the answer's body leaves Result-Code optional, as
;; SWx's do, Result-Code absent beside one in Experimental-Result under
;; the 3GPP Vendor-Id. The other answers print { Result-Code }, which
;; the sentence's absence contradicts (docs/constraints.md). Clause
;; 10.4.1 defines no transient code.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: swa-dea-4-2-2-1-2-result-code-permanent-failure
; AVP: Result-Code
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Command-Section: 4.2.2.1.2
; Section: 10.3.1
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"When one of the result codes defined here is included in a response, it shall be inside an Experimental-Result AVP and the Result-Code AVP shall be absent."
    exclude 5450, 5451, 5452, 5453, 5454, 5455, 5456, 5554


