;; The 3GPP AAA Server/Proxy - EIR reference point, clause 11: the
;; answer is TS 29.272's ME-Identity-Check-Answer, which this file does
;; not print, so no scope names it; TS 29.272's file reads the same
;; condition of it.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: eca-equipment-status
; AVP: Equipment-Status
; Section: 11.1.2.1.1
; Table: 11.1.2.1.1/2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"It shall be present if the result of the ME Identity Check is DIAMETER_SUCCESS."
    text-only


;; TS 29.272's ME-Identity-Check-Request, which this file does not
;; print; TS 29.272's file reads its Terminal-Information's IMEI and
;; Software-Version alone in ECR.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: eir-terminal-information
; AVP: Terminal-Information
; Section: 11.1.2.1.1
; Table: 11.1.2.1.1/1
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"Within this Information Element, only the IMEI and the Software-Version AVPs shall be used on the 3GPP AAA Server/Proxy"
    text-only


;; What traffic is of high priority, and the level, are the operator's.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: drmp-high-priority
; AVP: DRMP
; Section: D.2
; Versions: 18.6.0..19.2.0
"Diameter requests related to high priority traffic (e.g, MPS, emergency) shall contain a DRMP AVP with a high priority of which the level value is operator dependent."
    text-only
